{
  "info": {
    "name": "SwiftRide Gateway - Matching Events + Payment Events",
    "description": "RabbitMQ end-to-end scenario through YARP using DevelopmentJwt and mock payments. Requires Messaging:Transport=RabbitMQ on all three services, TripLifecycle:MatchingTransport=Events, and the messaging Compose profile. See docs/api-reference.md section 7. Select a Postman environment. Tokens, actor IDs, idempotency keys and trip snapshots persist in that environment for independent Send requests. Health does not reset the saved session. Use a fresh environment for a new full scenario. For Collection Runner, run all 20 requests in order, one iteration, delay 1000 ms, request timeout 15000 ms. Three polling steps stop after 30 pending responses each. Polling counters are run-local. Keep token values local; do not share or export populated environments. Verify broker activity and payment/ledger separately; HTTP results alone do not prove RabbitMQ delivery or a single charge.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:5080",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "url": "{{base_url}}/health",
        "description": "See docs/api-reference.md section 7. Select a Postman environment. Send independently with saved tokens and trip data, or use Collection Runner for the full workflow."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.variables.set('quote_polls', 0);",
              "pm.variables.set('paid_polls', 0);",
              "pm.variables.set('driver_polls', 0);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"01 Health\", function () {",
              "  try {",
              "pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
              "  } catch (error) {",
              "    pm.execution.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    throw error;",
              "  }",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Rider token",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "url": "{{base_url}}/dev/token?userId={{rider_id}}&role=rider",
        "description": "See docs/api-reference.md section 7. Select a Postman environment. Send independently with saved tokens and trip data, or use Collection Runner for the full workflow."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"02 Rider token\", function () {",
              "  try {",
              "pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
              "const token = pm.response.json().access_token;",
              "pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "pm.environment.set('rider_token', token);",
              "  } catch (error) {",
              "    pm.execution.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    throw error;",
              "  }",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
